  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Planplansje",
    "overview": "The room is published as a plate in a Nordic architecture journal. An ink masthead sits over a cool stone plate; the plan is drawn on it with solid ink poché walls and a hairline metre grid; a page-white side page on the right carries the catalogue, the numbered key and the totals, separated by ink rules. The interface is a two-value world, ink and paper, and the single NOVOOI spot yellow marks only what is chosen or what saves.\n\nDensity is that of a printed plate key: fixed type steps, tabular numbers, rules instead of cards. The plan itself is the subject; chrome steps back to outlined ink controls. This world deliberately replaces the incumbent white floating panels with soft shadows and a blue highlight.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two values (ink #17191A and page-white / stone) plus one spot (#EEFC9B).",
      "1px ink rules divide docked surfaces; shadow is reserved for things that float.",
      "4px corners on every control and surface.",
      "Four fixed type steps (11/13/15/20) in Season Sans; Gazpacho only for the plate title.",
      "Numbered key markers on the plan matched to numbered rows in the I rommet list."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Spot Rule",
        "body": "The spot yellow means \"chosen\" or \"save\". It never fills a panel, a heading or decoration; if nothing is selected and nothing is unsaved, the only spot on screen is the wordmark dot and the Lagre button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Value Rule",
        "body": "Everything else is ink on paper or paper on ink. A pressed state inverts to ink; it does not introduce a new hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Steps Rule",
        "body": "Interface text uses only 11, 13, 15 and 20px (`--t-xs/s/m/l`). The 28px plate title and 12px key numbers are the only exceptions.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Serif Rule",
        "body": "Gazpacho appears on the H1 `.plate-title` and nowhere else.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase or letter-spaced labels; labels are sentence case at 11px, weight 600, in graphite.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Areas, heights, prices, counts and key numbers use tabular numerals; totals align right.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rules-Not-Shadows Rule",
        "body": "If a surface is docked, it gets an ink rule and no shadow. Shadow means \"this floats over the plate\".",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** separate docked regions with 1px ink rules (#17191A) and keep them shadowless.",
      "**Do** keep every interface size on the 11/13/15/20px steps.",
      "**Do** invert pressed states to ink with page-white text.",
      "**Do** read the canvas colours from `--stage`, `--cap`, `--accent` and `--grid` so the plan and the chrome stay one print job.",
      "**Do** number every placed product on the plan and in the key list with the same circular badge.",
      "**Do** use tabular figures for measures, prices and counts."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use the spot yellow for anything except selection, the save action, active tools and key markers.",
      "**Don't** set Gazpacho anywhere but the plate title H1.",
      "**Don't** use uppercase or tracked-out labels.",
      "**Don't** round corners beyond 4px on controls and panels (6px on dialogs only).",
      "**Don't** put a shadow on a docked surface or a card hover.",
      "**Don't** reintroduce a blue highlight or blue measurement lines."
    ]
  }
}